<title>CHINA: China provinces predict bumper summer harvests.</title>
<headline>China provinces predict bumper summer harvests.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Officials in China's central province of Anhui are predicting a record summer wheat harvest of 9.0 million tonnes in 1997, the Xinhua news agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Rapeseed output in the province was expected to total more than 1.3 million tonnes, it said but gave no comparative figures.</p>
<p>Officials in neighbouring Hubei province expected a bumper summer grain harvest this year, with output to hit 5.0 million tonnes -- up 300,000 tonnes compared with 1996, Xinhua said in a separate report.</p>
<p>Production of summer edible oil in Hubei was expected to reach 1.4 million tonnes, up 51,200 tonnes compared with 1996, the agency said but did not elaborate.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
